 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the \"CountingMeasure\" and the \"RiemannianMeasure\" of a ball, shell or \
tube; the profiles are its Table over the radius"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"b6de93ca-4ea3-4605-b769-986f1d7cc3a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A region on a graph is measured by counting vertices, and its boundary is \
not negligible at a finite scale: the vertices at distance exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74d5f653-da5c-48b1-84bc-88c246cad67d"],
 " are a share of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69780188-de3b-42ad-97dd-15cd1dcbdb43"],
 " of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96b91601-8a2d-4a90-9072-4980dc3a7695"],
 ". So every region carries two measures. The counting measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0238411e-b717-4c5a-9516-7b9e8f2e21be"],
 ". The Riemannian measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fc5ecab-5446-47ee-9252-bca3144455fe"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], "=", "{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[SubsetEqual]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c10043c9-a6d4-4e83-9e06-aed28a50f641"],
 " is the set of vertices all of whose neighbours lie in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "242d307f-c356-4ca2-afe0-23ca64fdb8bb"],
 "; it is the count without the boundary and the default of the growth \
estimators."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e774e552-6e52-4e94-921c-366c594aa551"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f215281-12c3-4620-9582-5156bdabd47c"],
 " has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a89f2925-e92a-4211-abc9-afa79143413c"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21ccfc12-d9c9-45c0-8807-80bb521b873e"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b9e18fed-0d47-4f0c-9f62-fd6f9e19f0ee"],
 "; the shell has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51d0ed7d-b8b6-4d00-ae7c-7edbcdd6f383"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "babe8085-8ca6-45ae-adf8-7dff5155b59f"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular lattice before the rim, the \
convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"48774606-28df-4fea-b249-96d9fc4403c8"],

